From 0a7e7a29efa084e6cdfc4cb47b31dd5226e47324 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sn3ro <zak.darek@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 22:26:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ui): ortho pick rays start at the near plane, not the eye
 plane

PR #1689 moved the orthographic near plane far behind the eye (the ortho
eye sits only ORTHO_EYE_DIST = 100 mm in front of the target), but
Camera::ray_through still started the ray on the eye plane. A face nearer
the viewer than the eye plane was drawn but not pickable: a top-view click
on a 300 mm column went through its top face and selected its bottom.

One helper, Camera::ortho_behind_eye, now gives the near-plane offset to
both mvp (where it clips) and ray_through (where the ray starts). The ray
keeps its line and direction, so the cursor closure, the ortho dolly and
the plane-intersecting drags are unchanged.

Pinned by ortho_pick_tests:
an_ortho_pick_hits_the_top_face_that_stands_above_the_eye_plane,
the_ortho_ray_starts_on_the_near_plane_and_keeps_its_line.

Fixes #2375

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
